(50, 3, 'ihxmanny@gmail.com', 'assistant', 'How about trying a simple beef gravy recipe? Here’s a basic one you can follow:\n\n**Ingredients:**\n- 500g beef, cut into cubes\n- 1 onion, chopped\n- 2 tomatoes, chopped\n- 2-3 cloves of garlic, minced\n- 1-inch piece of ginger, minced\n- 2-3 tablespoons of cooking oil\n- 1 teaspoon cumin seeds\n- 1 teaspoon garam masala\n- Salt to taste\n- Fresh coriander for garnish\n\n**Instructions:**\n1. Heat the oil in a pot over medium heat. Add cumin seeds and let them sizzle.\n2. Add the chopped onion and sauté until golden brown.\n3. Stir in the minced garlic and ginger and cook for another minute.\n4. Add the beef cubes and cook until they are browned on all sides.\n5. Add the chopped tomatoes, garam masala, and salt. Mix well and let it cook until the tomatoes soften.\n6. Add enough water to cover the beef, bring to a boil, then reduce heat and let it simmer until the beef is tender (about 1-1.5 hours).\n7. Once the beef is cooked, adjust seasoning if necessary, and garnish with fresh coriander.\n\nServe it hot with chapati. Enjoy your meal!', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-26 06:20:34', NULL),
